    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=You are an expert technical recruiter. Evaluate how well this resume fits the target role.\n\nTARGET ROLE: {{ $('Resume Upload Form').item.json.Role }}\n\nJOB DESCRIPTION (may be empty):\n{{ $json.job_description }}\n\nRESUME:\n{{ $('Extract Resume Text').item.json.text }}\n\nFollow these steps:\n1. Build the list of required skills for the target role. If a job description is given, take the required skills from it. If it is empty, list the 8 to 10 core skills normally required for the target role (tools, languages, frameworks, concepts). Put them in required_skills.\n2. Check the resume for each required skill. Count a skill as matched if there is clear evidence: skills section, project, internship, certification, coursework or experience. Do not assume skills that are not written.\n3. Fill matched_skills (required skills found) and missing_skills (required skills not found).\n4. Score from 0 to 100:\n   - 60 points: percentage of required skills matched\n   - 20 points: relevant projects and internships for this role\n   - 10 points: years of experience and depth\n   - 10 points: education and certifications\n5. Be fair to freshers. Give credit for related skills, coursework, projects, internships and certifications, not only exact tool names. If the resume is from a clearly different field than the target role, score below 50. If it partly overlaps, score by the overlap.\n6. recommendation must be exactly one of: Shortlist (score 70 or more), Maybe (45 to 69), Reject (below 45).\n7. Ignore name, gender, age and college name while scoring.\n8. If the resume text is empty or unreadable, return match_score 0, recommendation Reject, and say so in gaps.\n9. Do not invent any detail. If email or phone is missing, return an empty string.\n10. strengths and gaps: maximum 2 short sentences each, specific to the target role.",
        "hasOutputParser": true,
        "options": {}
      },
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.agent",
      "typeVersion": 3.1,
      "position": [
        496,
        16
      ],
      "id": "22c2e0fc-f4c0-4ed5-9021-ff004f121bd5",
